 {"id": "README-008", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P5", "title": "P5 \u2014 the Development block omits 'make spec-check' (a gate ci.yml runs), and the repo-layout table describes ci.yml as 'build, vet, test' only", "reasoning": "Doc severity P5 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (coverage/polish; doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) \u2014 policy, not a new assessment.\n\nTHE DEFECT: the Development block omits a gate CI actually runs, so a contributor cannot reproduce the CI gate set from the README \u2014 and a gate that lands without a README line stays invisible.\n\n.github/workflows/ci.yml steps, in order: Build (go build ./...), Vet (go vet ./...), Gofmt (go test -count=1 -run TestGofmt ./internal/fmtcheck), Version-check (internal/versioncheck), Spec-check (go test -count=1 ./internal/speccheck), Install govulncheck v1.7.0, Vulnerability-check (internal/vulncheck), Test (go test -short -count=1 ./...).\n\nREADME.md:1153-1160 lists: go build ./cmd/boardctl, go test ./..., make fmt-check, make version-check, make vuln-check, make release. grep -n 'spec-check' README.md -> no match. make spec-check (Makefile:78; runs go test -count=1 ./internal/speccheck) was executed in this sweep -> \"ok github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/internal/speccheck\" (rc=0), so the target is real, green, and unmentioned.\nREADME.md:1127 describes the same workflow as \"CI (build, vet, test)\", under-describing its gate set.\n\nFIX: add a `make spec-check` line to the Development block (README.md:1153-1160) with the one-line purpose \u2014 the serve/OpenAPI parity gate CI enforces (docs/muster/openapi.yaml vs the serve wiring) \u2014 and update the ci.yml row at README.md:1127 to name the real steps.\nACCEPTANCE: every gate ci.yml runs is runnable from the Development block, and README.md:1127's description matches ci.yml's steps.\n\nVERIFIED THIS SWEEP (so the row does not overstate): make fmt-check rc=0, make version-check rc=0, make vuln-check rc=0 (govulncheck pin alrea