 {"id": "README-009", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P5", "title": "P5 \u2014 README.md:1216 states the go.mod toolchain pin as \"go 1.26.6\"; go.mod:3 declares \"go 1.26.9\" (BT-080 bumped the directive 2026-10-09 and left the README sentence stale)", "reasoning": "Doc severity P5 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) \u2014 that is policy, not a new assessment of this defect. Class: accuracy (a documented value that contradicts the file the README names as its source).\n\nTHE DEFECT\nREADME.md:1216-1219 (section \"Deployment freshness gate (BT-057)\") states the repo's toolchain pin and names the file that carries it, and the value it names is no longer in that file:\n\n  README.md:1216  \"The toolchain requirement: go.mod declares `go 1.26.6`. The Go 1.26.5 standard library shipped reachable advisories that 1.26.6 fixes \u2014 `net/http` (GO-2026-6089), `crypto/tls` (GO-2026-6090) and `encoding/asn1` (GO-2026-5972) \u2014 so a lower `go` directive, or a build with an older toolchain, fails this gate.\"\n\nEXACT COMMANDS AND OUTPUT (2026-10-17, HEAD 94e5b56, which is origin/main; probe log /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/boardctl/probe-go-version-20261017.log)\n  grep -n '1\\.26' README.md\n    -> 1216:The toolchain requirement: go.mod declares `go 1.26.6`. ...\n  sed -n '3p' go.mod\n    -> go 1.26.9\n  git log --format='%ad %h %s' --date=short -L 3,3:go.mod\n    -> 2026-10-09 3c83aa8 fix(vuln): bump go 1.26.6 -> 1.26.9 \u2014 7 reachable stdlib vulns (net/http, crypto/tls, net/textproto, mime/multipart)\n    -> 2026-09-17 08655c4 fix: pin the toolchain to go 1.26.6 and add the dependency-vulnerability gate. Addresses BT-033.\n\nCAUSE (both rows complete, so nothing is pending on the code side)\nThe paragraph was written for BT-033 (2026-09-18, commit 08655c4), when `go 1.26.6` really was the pin. BT-080 (P1, complete 2026-10-09, commit 3c83aa8) bumped the directive to 1.26.9 and left README.md:1216 alone. The sentence is now false in two ways: the value it names, and the advisory list behind it (the 1.26.9 bump cleared GO-2026-6603/6607/6608/6611/6612/6613/6617 \u2014 7 advisories \u2014 not the 3 named here).\n\nWHY NO GATE CATCHES IT\ninternal/versioncheck is the repo's README gate, but it compares only README release-tag surfaces (`Current release: **vX.Y.Z**` and every /releases/download/<tag>/ URL); it never reads the `go` directive, and there is no `make docs-check`/`docs-drift` target. Verified: `grep -rn '1\\.26' internal/versioncheck/` -> no match; `grep -n 'docs-check' Makefile` -> no match; `make version-check` -> \"ok github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/internal/versioncheck\" (rc=0). So README-vs-go.mod drift is structurally unguarded while the gate is green.\n\nIMPACT\nA contributor who reads \"the requirement is 1.26.6\" and builds with GOTOOLCHAIN=local on a 1.26.6 toolchain meets the directive-mismatch the same paragraph tells them to respect; with the default GOTOOLCHAIN=auto the 1.26.9 toolchain is fetched silently, so the sentence misstates why their build behaves as it does.\n\nFIX (one line)\nREADME.md:1216 -> \"go.mod declares `go 1.26.9`\", and restate the following sentence for the current pin (the 1.26.9 bump cleared the 1.26.6-and-earlier reachable advisories). Keep the closing instruction (\"Do not lower the directive to silence the gate; raise it to the patched release instead\") unchanged.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n`grep -n '1\\.26' README.md` shows the value on README.md:1216 equal to the value on line 3 of go.mod, and the paragraph's advisory sentence no longer asserts a superseded patch level.\n\nUNVERIFIED\nThe GOTOOLCHAIN=local refusal on an actual 1.26.6 toolchain was NOT reproduced on this box (that toolchain is not installed); that sentence is read from README.md:1220-1222's own text, not measured here.\n\nRELATED ROWS\nBT-080 (complete \u2014 the bump that orphaned the sentence), BT-033 (complete \u2014 the bump the sentence was written for). No open 