 {"id": "DOC-35", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "title": "P4 \u2014 document the two uncited `header` setters (--set-ticks-idle, --set-last-tick) and define the header object's keys in README", "reasoning": "Doc severity P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (missing reference; doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) -- policy, not a new assessment.\n\nTHE DEFECT: the `header` command registers four setters (cmd/boardctl/main.go:1114 --set-ticks-total, :1115 --set-ticks-idle, :1116 --set-last-commit, :1117 --set-last-tick) and its own usage text lists all four (cmd/boardctl/main.go:1121). The README documents only two: `header --set-ticks-total 42 --set-last-commit abc1234` (README.md:130-131). `--set-ticks-idle` and `--set-last-tick` appear in NO repo doc (README/docs/skills each 0 hits for --set-last-tick; --set-ticks-idle has 1 hit in skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md:266 only). Related and unfixed in the same file: the header OBJECT the docs keep referencing is never defined in README - `ticks_idle`, `cooldown_s` and `last_tick` have 0 hits in README.md while README's doctor section reasons about header counters (README.md:202-225 \"Headerless boards\").\n\nEVIDENCE (T3; scratch board /tmp/bt-docs-scratch2, target repo untouched):\n  $ boardctl -C $S header --set-ticks-idle 3 --set-last-tick \"2026-10-17 12:00:00\"\n  header updated (line 1 of board.jsonl): ticks_idle, last_tick, updated_at\n  $ boardctl -C $S header --json\n  {\"project\":\"scratch2\",\"namespace\":\"scratch2\",\"version\":1,\"ticks_total\":0,\"ticks_idle\":3,\"cooldown_s\":21600,\"last_commit\":null,\"last_tick\":\"2026-10-17 12:00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"...\"}\n  $ grep -c 'ticks_idle\\|cooldown_s\\|last_tick' README.md   ->  0\n  $ grep -c -- '--set-last-tick' README.md docs/ skills/    ->  0\nArtifact: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md\n\nARTIFACT TO WRITE: README.md - extend the header block (README.md:129-135) with the two missing setters, and add the header key list (project, namespace, version, ticks_total, ticks_idle, cooldown_s, last_commit, last_tick, updated_at) with the type/default of each, sourced from the `header --json` output above.\nREADER: operator (3am recovery of a stale counter, README.md doctor section sends them at the header) and integrator (the header object is the board's only non-row JSON).\nACCEPT: README names all four --set-* flags; the header object's keys are enumerated with the default of each; a reviewer re-runs `header --json` on a scratch board and finds exactly the documented key set.\n\nch:trace row=DOC-35 spec=none:audit-lane-finding test=none:doc-gap doc=README.md#usage evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md witness=none:no-external-surface verdict=none:audit-lane commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=none:audit-lane task=document header setters and the header object", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.457592+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.457592+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "a57f8b382e356b3b21945b530ace40ab78047cf5fa747636632dafc552f4edd6"}, "foreman_note": null}
 {"id": "DOC-36", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "title": "P4 \u2014 document `list --all` / `stats --all`: fixture rows are HIDDEN by default, so census counts do not match the file", "reasoning": "Doc severity P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (missing reference; doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) -- policy, not a new assessment.\n\nTHE DEFECT: `list --all` and `stats --all` are registered (cmd/boardctl/main.go:503 and :1558, both `\"include fixture rows (ids in fixtures.jsonl)\"` / `\"include fixture rows\"`) and both are listed in the subcommand usage text, but `--all` appears in NO README line: `grep -c -- '--all' README.md` = 0 (it is documented only in skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md:93-94 and docs/specs/board-analytics-report.md:209,547). The consequence is not cosmetic: the default read path SILENTLY EXCLUDES every fixture row, so an operator counting rows on a board whose fixtures.jsonl carries entries sees a total that does not match `wc -l tasks.jsonl`, with nothing in the reference explaining the gap. README discusses fixtures.jsonl and \"fixture orphans\" in the doctor section (README.md:69-76) but never connects it to the read filters.\n\nEVIDENCE (T3; scratch board /tmp/bt-docs-scratch2, target repo untouched - fixtures.jsonl there carries the NEVER-DONE fixture row):\n  $ boardctl -C $S list            -> 2 task lines (SCR-0, SCR-1)      [NEVER-DONE fixture hidden]\n  $ boardctl -C $S list --all      -> 3 task lines (NEVER-DONE, SCR-0, SCR-1)\n  $ boardctl -C $S stats           -> \"by status: pending 1\"\n  $ boardctl -C $S stats --all     -> \"by status: pending 2\", \"P3 1\" added\nArtifact: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md\n\nARTIFACT TO WRITE: README.md, the read/usage section for `list` and `stats` (README.md:62-84) plus the fixtures discussion it already carries.\nREADER: operator (row counts that disagree with the file) and integrator (the census API's default exclusion).\nACCEPT: README states that `list`/`stats` exclude fixtures.jsonl ids by default and that `--all` includes them, with the observed 2-vs-3 line difference quoted.\n\nch:trace row=DOC-36 spec=none:audit-lane-finding test=none:doc-gap doc=README.md#usage evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md witness=none:no-external-surface verdict=none:audit-lane commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=none:audit-lane task=document list/stats --all fixture inclusion", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.482003+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.482003+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "557c90311108aea2c236df993155cc2c169f1bd9f3f416ff2d591ffb46e0284f"}, "foreman_note": null}
